      "message": "fix(post): write G49 before the program-end retract when G43.4 is active\n\nA section that tilts and then stands upright again ends with no rotary\nheld off zero. uprightAtEnd() then writes nothing, and onClose wrote\nG91 G28 Z0 while G43.4 was still active. A reference return is not\npermitted in G43.4 mode (FANUC 30i B-63944EN/02), so the control alarms.\n\nThe Fanuc and Doosan DNM posts now remember in endPreamble that the\nlast section left G43.4 on (tcpmLeft). onClose writes G49 before its\nown retract in that case. The other exits (a held rotary, a trailing\nGo home, the next preamble) already write G49 and are unchanged.\n\nThe recorded golden fanuc/rotary.nc (a tilted section that ends at\nA0 B0) recorded the defect. It gains one G49 line after M5.\n\nPinned by program_end::fanuc_cancels_tcpm_before_program_end_after_a_tilt_back_to_zero\nand program_end::doosan_cancels_tcpm_before_program_end_after_a_tilt_back_to_zero\n(upright_after_tilt), and by script_fanuc rotary.\n\nFixes #4348\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
